Key Results / Physical Interpretation

- Star-forming fraction peaks strongly during merger-driven pericentre
  passages, consistent with tidal compression triggering collapse.

- Toomre Q shows clear episodic instability (Q < 1) aligned with orbital
  encounters, indicating bursty star formation conditions.

- Sérsic index increases over time toward n ≈ 4, consistent with transition
  from disk-like to elliptical-like remnant structure.

- Effective radius evolution shows progressive compaction of the merger
  remnant.

- Cumulative SF proxy exhibits accelerated growth during interaction phases,
  consistent with starburst-like behavior.

